<section class="page-hero page-hero--compact">
  <p class="eyebrow">{{workspace.organization}}</p>
  <h1>Organization identity.</h1>
  <p>Anyone can name an organization anything. A verified domain is what lets a credential holder tell yours from somebody who typed the same name.</p>
</section>

<section class="band band--white">
  {{#if errorMessage}}
    <div class="callout callout--warning"><strong>Not accepted.</strong> <span>{{errorMessage}}</span></div>
  {{/if}}
  {{#if (eq checked "verified")}}
    <div class="callout callout--success"><strong>Domain verified.</strong> <span>Holders now see <strong>{{identity.domain}}</strong> beside your name.</span></div>
  {{/if}}
  {{#if (eq checked "failed")}}
    <div class="callout callout--warning">
      <strong>Not found yet.</strong>
      <span>
        {{#if (eq reason "no-record")}}No TXT record exists at that name yet. DNS changes can take anywhere from a minute to a few hours to propagate.{{/if}}
        {{#if (eq reason "mismatch")}}A TXT record exists but its value does not match. Check for a stray space or a truncated paste.{{/if}}
        {{#if (eq reason "lookup-failed")}}The lookup itself failed. That usually means the domain has no nameservers responding.{{/if}}
        {{#if (eq reason "misplaced")}}The record exists, but at <code>{{identity.challenge.misplacedAt}}</code> — one level too high. Your provider appended the zone to the Host you typed. Edit the record's Host to <code>{{identity.challenge.hostField}}</code> so it resolves as <code>{{identity.challenge.fullRecordName}}</code>.{{/if}}
      </span>
    </div>
  {{/if}}

  <div class="identity-layout">
    <div>
      <article class="identity-state {{#if identity.isVerified}}identity-state--verified{{/if}}">
        <p class="eyebrow">Current identity</p>
        <h2>{{identity.displayIdentity}}</h2>
        {{#if identity.isVerified}}
          <span class="pill pill--ok">Verified domain</span>
          <p>Proven on {{identity.verifiedAt}}. This is what holders see.</p>
        {{else}}
          <span class="pill pill--muted">Unverified — system handle</span>
          <p>Your organization has a unique handle so it can always be identified, but holders are told the domain is unproven.</p>
        {{/if}}
        <dl class="identity-facts">
          <dt>Handle</dt><dd><code>{{identity.handle}}</code></dd>
          <dt>Public page</dt><dd><a href="{{identity.canonicalUrl}}">{{identity.canonicalUrl}}</a></dd>
          <dt>Identifier</dt><dd><code>{{identity.didWeb}}</code></dd>
        </dl>
      </article>

      {{#if showHosting}}
        <article class="identity-step">
          <h2>Serve Aegis ID from your domain</h2>
          {{#if hostingActive}}
            <p><span class="pill pill--ok">Live</span> Your organization is served at <a href="{{identity.hosting.baseUrl}}">{{identity.hosting.hostname}}</a>. Invitations, sign-in and the OIDC issuer all use it.</p>
            <form action="/organizations/{{subscriptionId}}/{{workspace.id}}/hosting" method="post" data-confirm-message="Stop serving Aegis ID from {{identity.hosting.hostname}}? Links revert to the platform host; credentials are untouched.">
              <input type="hidden" name="action" value="disable">
              <button class="button button--ghost" type="submit">Stop using this domain</button>
            </form>
          {{else if identity.hosting}}
            <p>Add these two records to the DNS for <strong>{{identity.hosting.hostname}}</strong>, then check. The certificate is issued automatically once the CNAME resolves.</p>
            <table class="data-table">
              <tbody>
                <tr><th>CNAME</th><td><code>{{identity.hosting.hostname}}</code> → <code class="wrap-anywhere">{{identity.hosting.cnameTarget}}</code></td></tr>
                <tr><th>Status</th><td>{{hostingStatusLabel}}{{#if identity.hosting.lastError}} — <span class="table-note">{{identity.hosting.lastError}}</span>{{/if}}</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
            <div class="inline-actions">
              <form action="/organizations/{{subscriptionId}}/{{workspace.id}}/hosting" method="post">
                <input type="hidden" name="action" value="check">
                <button class="button button--primary button--blue" type="submit">Check DNS now</button>
              </form>
              <form action="/organizations/{{subscriptionId}}/{{workspace.id}}/hosting" method="post">
                <input type="hidden" name="action" value="disable">
                <button class="button button--ghost" type="submit">Cancel</button>
              </form>
            </div>
          {{else if customDomainAllowed}}
            <p>Your domain is verified. You can now serve the whole platform — sign-in, invitations, the OIDC issuer, your public page — from a hostname under it, under your own name and logo (set those under Branding).</p>
            <form class="subscribe-form subscribe-form--narrow" action="/organizations/{{subscriptionId}}/{{workspace.id}}/hosting" method="post">
              <input type="hidden" name="action" value="request">
              <div class="field-group">
                <label for="hostname">Hostname</label>
                <input id="hostname" name="hostname" type="text" placeholder="id.{{identity.domain}}" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" required>
                <p class="table-note">Must be <code>{{identity.domain}}</code> or a name under it.</p>
              </div>
              <button class="button button--primary button--blue" type="submit">Use this domain</button>
            </form>
          {{else}}
            <p>Your domain is verified. Serving the whole platform from a hostname under it — under your own name and logo — is an Enterprise feature. <a href="/plans">See plans</a>.</p>
          {{/if}}
        </article>
      {{/if}}

      {{#if identity.isPending}}
        <article class="identity-step">
          <h2>Publish this record</h2>
          <p>Add one TXT record to the DNS for <strong>{{identity.domain}}</strong>, then come back and check.</p>
          <table class="data-table">
            <tbody>
              <tr><th>Type</th><td><code>TXT</code></td></tr>
              <tr><th>Name / Host</th><td><code>{{identity.challenge.hostField}}</code><div class="table-note">{{#if identity.challenge.isSubdomain}}Your provider hosts the zone <strong>{{identity.challenge.zone}}</strong> and appends it to whatever you type, so the Host must carry the subdomain: <code>{{identity.challenge.hostField}}</code>, not just <code>{{identity.challenge.recordName}}</code>.{{else}}Most providers add your domain automatically.{{/if}} The full name must resolve as <code>{{identity.challenge.fullRecordName}}</code>.</div></td></tr>
              <tr><th>Value</th><td><code class="wrap-anywhere">{{identity.challenge.value}}</code></td></tr>
              <tr><th>TTL</th><td>Lowest your provider allows, while testing</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p class="table-note">Expires {{identity.challenge.expiresAt}}. {{#if identity.challenge.lastCheckedAt}}Last checked {{identity.challenge.lastCheckedAt}}.{{/if}}</p>

          <div class="inline-actions">
            <form action="/organizations/{{subscriptionId}}/{{workspace.id}}/domain" method="post">
              <input type="hidden" name="action" value="verify">
              <button class="button button--primary button--blue" type="submit">Check DNS now</button>
            </form>
            <a class="button button--ghost" href="/help/domain-verification" target="_blank" rel="noopener">How do I add this? ↗</a>
            <form action="/organizations/{{subscriptionId}}/{{workspace.id}}/domain" method="post">
              <input type="hidden" name="action" value="cancel">
              <button class="button button--ghost" type="submit">Cancel claim</button>
            </form>
          </div>
        </article>
      {{else}}
        <article class="identity-step">
          <h2>{{#if identity.isVerified}}Claim a different domain{{else}}Claim your domain{{/if}}</h2>
          <p>Enter the domain your organization is known by. We will give you one DNS record to publish.</p>
          <form class="subscribe-form subscribe-form--narrow" action="/organizations/{{subscriptionId}}/{{workspace.id}}/domain" method="post">
            <div class="field-group">
              <label for="domain">Domain</label>
              <input id="domain" name="domain" type="text" placeholder="contoso.com" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" required>
              <p class="table-note">Just the domain — no <code>https://</code>, no path.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="inline-actions">
              <button class="button button--primary button--blue" type="submit">Get my DNS record</button>
              <a class="button button--ghost" href="/help/domain-verification" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Setup guide ↗</a>
            </div>
          </form>
        </article>
      {{/if}}
    </div>

    <aside class="identity-aside">
      <div class="note-panel">
        <strong>Why this matters</strong>
        <span>Organization names are free text, and two subscribers can legitimately use the same one. Without a proven domain, a holder receiving an invitation has no way to distinguish you from somebody who typed your name.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note-panel">
        <strong>DNS only, never a file upload</strong>
        <span>Publishing under your domain's zone requires control of the zone. That is the thing worth proving — a file on a web server only proves control of that server.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="note-panel">
        <strong>Your handle does not change</strong>
        <span><code>{{identity.handle}}</code> is yours whether or not a domain is verified, and it survives a domain changing hands.</span>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>
